            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital course of your 41-year-old male patient, admitted on 04/01/2021 with confirmed SARS-CoV-2 infection. On admission, he presented with fever, dry cough, and progressive dyspnoea. Chest X-ray and CT thorax confirmed bilateral COVID-19 pneumonia. Blood tests revealed elevated inflammatory markers (CRP, ferritin, D-dimer). Arterial blood gas analysis demonstrated mild hypoxaemia requiring supplemental oxygen therapy. The patient was treated with dexamethasone, anticoagulation, and supportive intravenous fluids. Continuous pulse oximetry and vital sign monitoring were maintained throughout. Respiratory physiotherapy was initiated early. He showed gradual clinical improvement and was discharged home on 14/01/2021 in recovering condition. Please ensure follow-up within two weeks, including repeat chest imaging if symptoms persist. Do not hesitate to contact me for further information.</div>"
            },
